  "condition": "Tool-free Windows x64 dispatch edits; one response then 4,212 shared oracle cases. Only the reference changed. Each round reversed order by task.",
  "examples_guide": "Native H0 Tape UTF-8. Header `N[name|-private|+extern]`, unnamed entry returns exit status. Args a,b,…, `'ab` shared byte views, `\"cd` mutable; shared before mutable. LF or `;;` separates functions outside literals and comments. Keep imports `>+IDs` and section order. SP separates instructions; TAB separates adjacent numbers, block counts, and named calls from identifier/digit operands. `:fn<TAB>ab` calls with a,b; numeric calls use source order, `:<`/`:>` neighbors, `::` self. Mutable call views disjoint.\n\nPrefix u64 wrapping `+-*/%&^|<>EDLGSTAO` add/sub/mul/div/rem/and/xor/or/lt/gt/eq/ne/le/ge/shl/shr/lazy-and/or; `!` not, `N` negate, `~` bitnot, `\\i` lazy cond/yes/no. `bx` binds or sets b; `+bx` adds x; `Yx` discards; tail x or `.x` returns. `?x` guards one statement, `?x<TAB>N[<TAB>M]` then N and optional else M. `@n<TAB>N` loop 0..<n with index in next free register; `Wx` while. Nested statements count once. Block locals end at exit; assignments to outer registers persist. `'` breaks, backtick continues. `1sum b0 @a<TAB>1 +bc b` sums 0..<a.\n\n`Za` len, `Bab` byte, `Xabc` store byte c at b, `Vabc` slice [b:c), `\\vab` tail, `bMn` zero buffer. `Kab` splits mutable a for the next statement into two new registers, suspending a. `\\B2/4/8` LE load(view,offset); `\\Q2/4/8` store(mut,offset,value). `\\b\"…\"` UTF-8 bytes, escapes `\\0\\n\\r\\t\\\"\\\\\\xHH`. `1head'a ?<Za4.0 \\B4a0` reads LE u32. Max u64 is `수`.\n\nSyntax examples (replace ⇥ with TAB). `2min ?<ab.a b` returns a when a<b, otherwise b. `2odd \\i&b1a0` returns a only for odd b. `1nested b0 @a⇥2 ?Ec0⇥2 +b1 +b2 +b4 b` returns 11 for a=2; the guard and its two inner instructions count as ONE instruction of the loop. `0 .:min⇥9⇥5` exits 5; a TAB separates the two numeric operands. `2pick'a ?LZab.0 Bab` returns 0 out of bounds, otherwise byte b. A function of arity 2 with header `2pick'a` has byte view a and scalar b.\n\nCompiler checkout CORE.md and AGENTS.md for details. Modes 19 glyph map, 20/21/22 scoped std, 30/31/32 checks Windows/Linux/RV64. Mode 47 builds/checks an ordered path list preceded by the target mode, one LF per line. Mode 50 takes target, function selector, then paths to find the original section and calls.\n",
